quran[11]{c,v,t}:
  29,64,"The life of this word is nothing but diversion and play. As for the abode of the Hereafter, it is indeed the (real) life if only they knew."
  29,65,"Whenever they board a ship, they call upon Allah, devoting (their) faith exclusively to Him. But, once He has delivered them safely to land, behold, they start ascribing partners (to Him again)."
  29,66,"So let them be ungrateful for what We have granted them. And let them enjoy themselves. Soon, they will know (the truth)."
  29,67,"And do they (i.e. the Meccan disbelievers) not see that We have made (the city of Mecca) a secure sanctuary, whereas people are being snatched away all around them? Would they still believe in falsehood and be ungrateful towards the blessing of Allah?"
  29,68,Who is more unjust than one who fabricates a lie against Allah or denies the truth after it has reached him? Is not the (final) abode of the disbelievers in Hell?
  29,69,"As for those who strive hard for Us, We shall surely guide them in Our ways. And Allah is indeed with the virtuously excellent."
  30,1,"Alif, Lam, Mim."
  30,2,"The Romans have been defeated,"
  30,3,"in a land nearby. But after their defeat, they will become victorious,"
  30,4,"within a few years. All command belongs to Allah, before and after. And on that day, the believers will rejoice,"
  30,5,"upon Allah’s help. He helps whom He pleases. And He is the All-Mighty, the All-Merciful."
